40 0 obj
<<
/ActualText (Flowchart illustrating data processing steps for Node k in the Anchored-SMR model, including variable definitions and iterative updates. The diagram presents a flowchart for data processing at Node k within the Anchored-SMR framework. It starts with "Node k data," comprising two sets: \({y_i, i ? I_k}\) and \({x_i, i ? I_k}\). Arrows lead to the "TMR" section, where initial calculations for \(n_k\), \(bar{y}_k\), and \(bar{x}_k\) are made. A central \(tilde{beta}\) is initialized, followed by iterative updates linked to derived parameters. The flowchart details how intermediate calculations contribute to the final outputs in the "Anchored-SMR" box, showcasing relationships and sequences vital for understanding the algorithm's functionality.)
/A 257 0 R
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/S /Figure
/T ()
/Pg 15 0 R
/Alt (Flowchart illustrating data processing steps for Node k in the Anchored-SMR model, including variable definitions and iterative updates. The diagram presents a flowchart for data processing at Node k within the Anchored-SMR framework. It starts with "Node k data," comprising two sets: \({y_i, i ? I_k}\) and \({x_i, i ? I_k}\). Arrows lead to the "TMR" section, where initial calculations for \(n_k\), \(bar{y}_k\), and \(bar{x}_k\) are made. A central \(tilde{beta}\) is initialized, followed by iterative updates linked to derived parameters. The flowchart details how intermediate calculations contribute to the final outputs in the "Anchored-SMR" box, showcasing relationships and sequences vital for understanding the algorithm's functionality.)
>>
endobj
41 0 obj
<<
/ActualText (Multi-panel figure: \(a\) Box plot of log2\(RMSE\) for TMR vs MR across Fine, Middle, and None conditions; \(b\) Line graphs for Rep-Challenged and Rep-Favored scenarios over iterations; \(c\) Line graphs for IID Random, Label Skew, and Rep-Favored strategies; \(d\) Grid of log2\(RMSE\) trends over iterations with varying delays and ratios. This figure consists of four panels examining log2\(RMSE\) across various conditions. Panel \(a\) shows a box plot comparing log2\(RMSE\) for TMR, MR, and Full methods categorized by Fine, Middle, and None, with TMR displaying the lowest values. Panel \(b\) features line graphs for Rep-Challenged and Rep-Favored scenarios, illustrating RMSE trends against iterations, where Rep-Favored consistently performs better. In Panel \(c\), three line graphs depict IID Random, Label Skew, and Rep-Favored partitioning strategies across iterations, showing differing performance rates. Panel \(d\) presents a grid of line graphs tracking log2\(RMSE\) across varying delays \(1, 2, 3\) and ratios \(10%, 30%, 50%\), highlighting error rate differences based on these conditions.)
/A 258 0 R
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/S /Figure
/T ()
/Pg 18 0 R
/Alt (Multi-panel figure: \(a\) Box plot of log2\(RMSE\) for TMR vs MR across Fine, Middle, and None conditions; \(b\) Line graphs for Rep-Challenged and Rep-Favored scenarios over iterations; \(c\) Line graphs for IID Random, Label Skew, and Rep-Favored strategies; \(d\) Grid of log2\(RMSE\) trends over iterations with varying delays and ratios. This figure consists of four panels examining log2\(RMSE\) across various conditions. Panel \(a\) shows a box plot comparing log2\(RMSE\) for TMR, MR, and Full methods categorized by Fine, Middle, and None, with TMR displaying the lowest values. Panel \(b\) features line graphs for Rep-Challenged and Rep-Favored scenarios, illustrating RMSE trends against iterations, where Rep-Favored consistently performs better. In Panel \(c\), three line graphs depict IID Random, Label Skew, and Rep-Favored partitioning strategies across iterations, showing differing performance rates. Panel \(d\) presents a grid of line graphs tracking log2\(RMSE\) across varying delays \(1, 2, 3\) and ratios \(10%, 30%, 50%\), highlighting error rate differences based on these conditions.)
>>
